<title>POLAND: Polish food prices rise 1.4 pct in Sept 1-10.</title>
<headline>Polish food prices rise 1.4 pct in Sept 1-10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish food prices rose 1.4 percent in the September 1-10 period after falling 0.1 percent in the previous 10 days and were 1.3 percent higher than in the August 1-10 period, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.  </p>
<p>				   SEPT 1-10   AUG 21-30   LAST 30 DAYS</p>
<p>POLISH FOOD PRICES (AVG)	1.4	  -0.1	 1.3   (0.1)</p>
<p> Bread				0.1	   0.1	 0.5   (0.8)</p>
<p> Fruit and vegetables	  -2.2	  -8.2     -13.3 (-16.1)</p>
<p> Meat and meat-products	 3.8	   1.6	 6.2   (3.8)</p>
<p> Dairy products		   0.3	   0.1	 0.5   (0.3)</p>
<p> Eggs				 3.5	   2.8	 9.2  (12.7)</p>
<p>NOTE: In brackets figures for the previous 30-day period ending on August 30.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
